apt 2.7.14 apt-pkg: use getservbyport() on musl/OHOS (no glibc _r variant)

srvrec.cc uses glibc's reentrant getservbyport_r().  OHOS ships musl,
which does not provide the _r variant -- the link fails with:

  undefined symbol: getservbyport_r

SRV lookups are infrequent; fall back to the POSIX non-reentrant
getservbyport() under musl (thread-safe in musl) and keep the glibc path
unchanged.  Verified on the OHOS build: links and resolves srv records.

--- a/apt-pkg/contrib/srvrec.cc
+++ b/apt-pkg/contrib/srvrec.cc
@@ -49,7 +49,15 @@
    struct servent *s_ent = nullptr;
    std::vector<char> buf(1024);
 
+#if defined(__GLIBC__)
    res = getservbyport_r(htons(port), "tcp", &s_ent_buf, buf.data(), buf.size(), &s_ent);
+#else
+   // OHOS/musl 没有 glibc 的 getservbyport_r 重入版；SRV 查询不频繁，用
+   // POSIX 非重入版 getservbyport 代替（musl 线程安全）。
+   (void)s_ent_buf; (void)buf;
+   s_ent = getservbyport(htons(port), "tcp");
+   res = (s_ent == nullptr) ? -1 : 0;
+#endif
    if (res != 0 || s_ent == nullptr)
       return false;
 
